  "id": "Compound::DB01148 - Gene::5141",
  "verbalization": "Flavoxate is shown to interact with Pde8a, Pde8b, and Pde4c, all of which are involved in 3',5'-cyclic-AMP phosphodiesterase activity. This activity is a key regulator of intracellular cyclic AMP levels, which are implicated in various physiological and pathological processes. The evidence suggests that Flavoxate may inhibit Pde4a through a mechanism involving its interaction with these related phosphodiesterases. The final scores from the paths indicate a consistent and plausible relationship, with the shared involvement of 3',5'-cyclic-AMP phosphodiesterase activity as a central node. The mechanism appears to be based on Flavoxate's ability to bind to and modulate the activity of these enzymes, which in turn affects Pde4a. The integrated evidence supports a mechanistic link between Flavoxate and Pde4a, mediated through the regulation of cyclic AMP levels via the phosphodiesterase pathway.",
